IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fra-recruiting`

-- Foreign Recruiting Act 1875, ss 2 to 5 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_foreign-recruiting-act-1875.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `Fixtures`

`an agent in Singapore signing up soldiers for a foreign army` MEANS Recruitment WITH
    `recruiting for` IS `a recognised foreign government`
    `the recruiter is within the limits of Singapore` IS TRUE
    `obtaining or attempting to obtain recruits` IS TRUE

`the same agent working from across the Causeway` MEANS Recruitment WITH
    `recruiting for` IS `a recognised foreign government`
    `the recruiter is within the limits of Singapore` IS FALSE
    `obtaining or attempting to obtain recruits` IS TRUE

`a foreign official in Singapore who is not seeking recruits` MEANS Recruitment WITH
    `recruiting for` IS `a recognised foreign government`
    `the recruiter is within the limits of Singapore` IS TRUE
    `obtaining or attempting to obtain recruits` IS FALSE

`an agent in Singapore trying to sign up fighters for a self-proclaimed government abroad` MEANS Recruitment WITH
    `recruiting for` IS `an authority assuming to exercise the powers of government over a people abroad`
    `the recruiter is within the limits of Singapore` IS TRUE
    `obtaining or attempting to obtain recruits` IS TRUE

`an agent in Singapore hiring guards for a private foreign security company` MEANS Recruitment WITH
    `recruiting for` IS `a private foreign company`
    `the recruiter is within the limits of Singapore` IS TRUE
    `obtaining or attempting to obtain recruits` IS TRUE

`a recruiter for a foreign army where no order has been made` MEANS Conduct WITH
    `the order` IS `no order`
    `the service is of` IS `a recognised foreign government`
    `induces or attempts to induce a person to accept, agree to accept, or proceed to a place to obtain a commission or employment` IS TRUE
    `aids the engagement of a person so induced by forwarding, conveying, advancing money or otherwise` IS FALSE
    `acts knowingly` IS TRUE

`the same recruiter after a Gazette general prohibition` MEANS Conduct WITH
    `the order` IS `a general prohibition notified in the Gazette under section 4`
    `the service is of` IS `a recognised foreign government`
    `induces or attempts to induce a person to accept, agree to accept, or proceed to a place to obtain a commission or employment` IS TRUE
    `aids the engagement of a person so induced by forwarding, conveying, advancing money or otherwise` IS FALSE
    `acts knowingly` IS TRUE

`a recruiter personally prohibited by a section 3 order` MEANS Conduct WITH
    `the order` IS `a section 3 order prohibiting this person`
    `the service is of` IS `a recognised foreign government`
    `induces or attempts to induce a person to accept, agree to accept, or proceed to a place to obtain a commission or employment` IS TRUE
    `aids the engagement of a person so induced by forwarding, conveying, advancing money or otherwise` IS FALSE
    `acts knowingly` IS TRUE

`the prohibited recruiter's assistant, who is not named in the order` MEANS Conduct WITH
    `the order` IS `a section 3 order prohibiting another person only`
    `the service is of` IS `a recognised foreign government`
    `induces or attempts to induce a person to accept, agree to accept, or proceed to a place to obtain a commission or employment` IS FALSE
    `aids the engagement of a person so induced by forwarding, conveying, advancing money or otherwise` IS TRUE
    `acts knowingly` IS TRUE

`a permitted recruiter who breaks a condition of the permission` MEANS Conduct WITH
